iterations.reply:
I left out the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause is its entire authority, and it grants only `kb-read` and `tool-llm`. Adding `http-client` would widen that grant, which needs an updated graph type and a recorded approval, not just a changed body. The request would also send the raw question text to an external host in a URL. The files below implement the node as specified.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{conversation-context, response-result, agent-response, llm-error};

    import aap:caps/tool-llm@0.1.0;
    import aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(ctx: conversation-context) -> response-result;
}
```

